  <body xml:id="j003">
   

   <pb xml:id="leaf001r" facs="yal.00353.001_large.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <note type="editorial" place="top" hand="#h04">525</note>
   
   <metamark function="adjust" target="#j003"><add place="top" hand="#h04">Bourgeois</add></metamark>
   
   <note type="editorial" place="top" hand="#h04">Robson</note>
   
   <head type="main">W<del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike">H</del>ALT WHITMAN'S LAST<add place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a001">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a001">*</add><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03">&#8212;GOOD-BYE MY FANCY</del>.</head>
   <addSpan hand="#h03" spanTo="#a002"/><metamark function="adjust" target="#j001">&#182;</metamark><head type="sub" xml:id="j001">"Good Bye my Fancy"&#8212;concluding annex to <hi rend="underline">Leaves of Grass.</hi></head><metamark function="emphasize" target="#j001">)</metamark><metamark rend="marked"  function="adjust" target="#j001">in one line italic &amp; s c</metamark><anchor xml:id="a002"/>
   
   <metamark function="emphasize" target="#e001"><add hand="#h03">&#948;</add></metamark><p xml:id="e001">H. Heine's first principle<del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike" xml:id="d001">s</del><add place="right" hand="#h03"><metamark function="delete" target="d001"></metamark></add> of criticising a book was, <add hand="#h03"><metamark function="delete" target="#d002" place="left">&#948;</metamark></add>what motive<del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike" xml:id="d002">s</del> is the author trying to carry out, or express or accomplish? and the second, Has he achieve<subst><del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike">e</del><add place="right" xml:id="a004">'<metamark function="add" target="#a004">&#711;</metamark></add></subst>d<subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike">them</del><add place="above">it</add></subst>?</p>
   
   <metamark function="adjust" target="#j002"><add hand="#h03">&#182;</add></metamark><p xml:id="j002">The theory of <add hand="#h03" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a003" place="below">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a003">my</add>"Leaves of Grass" <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike">as an utterance or</del><add place="above">a</add></subst> composition of verses <add hand="#h03"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#d003">(</metamark></add><del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike" xml:id="d003">we are authentically informed</del><add hand="#h03"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#d003">)</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="left"><metamark function="delete" target="#d003"></metamark></add> has been from first to last, <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a005">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="top" rend="marked">(if I am to give impromptu a hint a hint of the spinal marrow of the business, and sign it with my name,)</add> to thoroughly possess the mind, memory, cognizance of the author himself<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a005">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="left" xml:id="a005">,<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a005">/</metamark></add> with everything beforehand<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a006">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="above" xml:id="a006">&#8212;<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a006">/</metamark></add>a full armory of concrete actualities, observations<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a007">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="above" xml:id="a007">,<metamark function="add" target="#a007">/</metamark></add> humanity, past poems, ballads, facts, technique<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a008">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="left" xml:id="a008">,<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a008">/</metamark></add> war and peace, politics<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a009">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="right" xml:id="a009">,<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a009">/</metamark></add> north and south<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a010">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="right" xml:id="a010">,<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a010">/</metamark></add> east and west, nothing too large or too small, the sciences as far as possible&#8212;and above all <gap reason="deleted" extent="one word"/> <subst><del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike" xml:id="d004">merits</del><add place="left" hand="#h03"><metamark function="delete" target="#d004"></metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03">America and</add></subst> the present&#8212;after and out of which the subject of the poem, long or short, has been invariably turned over to his <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike">e</del><add place="above">E</add></subst>motionality, even Personality, to be shaped thence; and <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike">thence</del><add place="above">strictly therefore</add></subst>emerges<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a011">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="right" xml:id="a011">,<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a011">/</metamark></add> with all its merits and demirits on its head. Every page of <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike">Walt Whitman's poetry</del><add place="below">&#8248;<add place="above">my poetic or attempt at poetic utterance</add></add></subst>, therefore smacks of the living physical identity, date, environment, individuality, probably beyond anything known<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a012">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="right" xml:id="a012">,<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a012">/</metamark></add> and in style often offensive to the conventio<subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">u</del><add place="right" xml:id="e002" seq="2">n<metamark function="emphasize" target="#e002">/</metamark></add></subst>s.</p>
   
   <metamark function="adjust" target="#j004"><add hand="#h03">&#182;</add></metamark><p xml:id="j004">This new last cluster<subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike">"</del><add place="below">,</add></subst> <add hand="#h03" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a013">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="above" xml:id="a013">"<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a013">/</metamark></add>Good-Bye my Fancy" follows suit, and yet with a difference. The clef is here changed to its lowest, and the little book is a lot of tremulos about old age, death, and faith. The <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">physic</del><add place="above" seq="2">physical</add></subst> just lingers<add hand="#h03" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a014">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="right" hand="#h03" xml:id="a014">,<metamark function="emphasize" target="#a014">/</metamark></add> but almost vanishes. <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">It</del><add place="above" xml:id="a015">The <del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike" seq="3">little</del> book</add></subst><add place="below" seq="2" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a015">&#8248;</metamark></add> is garrulous, irascible( like old Lear) and has various breaks and even tricks to avoid monotony. It will have to be ciphered<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a016">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="above" xml:id="a016">and ciphered</add> out long&#8212;and is <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a017"></metamark>&#8248;</add><add hand="#h03" place="above" xml:id="a017">notably</add> in some respects the most curious part of <add hand="#h03"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#e003"><del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike">(</del></metamark></add><add hand="#h03" place="left"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#e003">stet)</metamark></add><seg xml:id="e003">its author</seg><add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a018">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a018">,</add><add place="above" hand="#h03"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#a018">/</metamark></add>s<add hand="#h03"><metamark function="emphasize" target="e003"><del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike">)</del></metamark></add><add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#e003">. . . . .</metamark></add><del><add place="below" hand="#h03">my</add></del> curious works.</p>
   
<signed hand="#h03">Walt Whitman</signed>

<note place="bottom" type="archival" hand="#h04">Ha 154</note>
   
   
  
  
